@@ -2490,6 +2490,23 @@ Subtitles
     Subtitles in ASS format are normally not changed intentionally, but
     overriding them can be controlled with ``--sub-ass-override``.
 
+``--subtitle-layout=<yes|no>``
+    Enable collection of structured subtitle layout from the primary subtitle
+    renderer (default: no). The result is available through the
+    ``subtitle-layout`` command and the
+    ``subtitle-layout-revision`` property.
+
+    This requires a libass build with the layout API.
+    The initial supported source formats are ASS and SubRip. SubRip exercises
+    mpv's conversion into libass events; other converted text formats and
+    bitmap subtitle formats report ``unsupported-format``.
+
+    The API reports only the primary subtitle track in the ordinary OSD
+    output-render path. Subtitle filtering with ``vf=sub``, secondary
+    subtitles, stereo layouts, and ``--blend-subtitles=yes|video`` renders are
+    intentionally unsupported. Geometry describes the render selected by mpv;
+    it is not confirmation that the video output presented that frame.
+
 ``--sub-demuxer=<[+]name>``
     Force subtitle demuxer type for ``--sub-file``. Give the demuxer name as
     printed by ``--sub-demuxer=help``.
